  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **The Ocean*$** (1 review): Reggie Watts sang on it; reviewer disliked his attempt to imitate Robert Plant's wailing, preferring a more personal take [3]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **See in You**: mythic rare: 2 archived performances [4]\n- **Power Of Soul**: rare: 3 archived performances [4]\n- **Rverb**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **California Loving**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **Don't Tell**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 3 archived performances [4]\n- **New Song**: back after 54 archived shows (651 days); rare: 6 archived performances [4]\n- **It's Your Thing&**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **soulive2006-04-22.flac16** (recommended): source not stated; 14 songs; 103 min; rated 4.5/5 by 2 [1]. Said about its sound: Good sound quality, minimal crowd noise, and well balanced instruments [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- The show included a double encore [2]\n- The Ocean closed the show, according to the reviewer's correction [3]\n- Reviewer saw the band three times that year, once before as a trio, and judged this the best of them [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **soulive2006-04-22.flac16**: taped by Paul Davison; transferred by Paul Davison; source: studio projects c-4(cards, DIN)>Canare Starquad XLR>ua-5(digimod)>Nomad Jukebox 3 (16bit/44.1Hz) [1]",
